    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters the final stretch of the season with a high-ceiling lineup geared toward maximizing efficiency against favorable matchups. The premier play today is **Vinnie Pasquantino** (71.91), who benefits from a generous matchup against Tanner Bibee (4.49 xERA) and a massive 14-point boost from platoon dynamics. Right behind him, **James Wood** (71.49) remains an indispensable core piece; batting leadoff against Tong provides elite volume, and his underlying xwOBA of .404 suggests he is primed to capitalize on this start. **Corbin Carroll** (70.70) and **Josh Naylor** (70.49) also clear the 70-point threshold comfortably, with **Corbin Carroll** remaining our high-leverage weapon for stolen bases despite the slight efficiency drag caused by his opposing pitcher.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Griffin Conine**, who fell short of the 40-point \"zebra\" threshold with a score of 33.76. While his power upside is usually appealing, the matchup against Suter\u2014a left-handed specialist\u2014tanked his projection, exacerbated by a significant -9% platoon penalty. We are playing it safe to preserve game caps, keeping him benched in favor of **Mickey Moniak**, whose favorable platoon split against right-handed pitching anchors him at a solid 66.00. We are monitoring the status of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Isaac Paredes** closely; both are reliable starters today, but their scores reflect tight margins. As we continue to monitor the wire for **Jose Caballero**, **Trevor Story**, and **Seiya Suzuki**\u2014all of whom are out of action today\u2014the focus remains on maintaining our categorical lead through high-percentage plate appearances. Expect volatility, but keep faith in the model's preference for **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **James Wood** to carry the offensive load.",
